# Personal configuration stays local. The neutral template is tracked.
config.py

# Python bytecode.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Build products and historical archives are preserved on disk, but are not
# duplicated into Git history. Everything local now lives under Resources in
# named subfolders (August 9, 2026), so these rules point at whole folders
# rather than at individual files scattered through a mixed directory.
_Archive/
# Compiled output and PyInstaller scratch. Releases is the distribution
# channel, so nothing in here is worth versioning: the exe is attached to a
# release and the README that used to ship beside it had no reader once people
# started downloading a single file rather than a folder.
OSRS Dashboard Resources/Build/Output/
OSRS Dashboard Resources/Build/_build/
# Every package that has ever shipped, plus superseded build scripts. Pinned
# releases live here and are exempt from archive pruning.
OSRS Dashboard Resources/Shipped Builds/

# Workspace operating files describe how the project is worked on rather than
# how the dashboard works, and they stay on the local machine. Naming them one
# by one meant every new workspace file type published itself by default until
# someone remembered to add a line here, and the failure mode is a personal
# file going public. So markdown is excluded wholesale and publishing is
# opt-in: add a `!` line below for any doc genuinely meant for readers of the
# repository (CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/, a changelog).
*.md
!README.md

# Resources holds all local material for this project, in named subfolders per
# the create-project convention. What ships from it is the runtime assets at
# its top level — the pinned Chart.js and the four webfonts embedded into every
# generated dashboard — plus the build script under Build/. Each subfolder is
# uniformly published or local; nothing mixes at the file level.
OSRS Dashboard Resources/.gitkeep

# Local editor and operating-system noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
